  "status": "draft",
  "note": "Private test IPA 758, second request, for the maintainer's requests of 16 November 2026 after the IPA 756 test (\"Probl\u00e8me de FPS qui oscille, saccade, toujours artefacts violet mais bonne nouvelles plus de bloc noir\", then \"aide toi avec ce github : https://github.com/cheemu21/plumber-racer-2\"): the verified IPA 757 (run 43807403424, IPA effa19e0: the content of 756 with the NeoPlay Chromecast stage 2) with the S2Arm engine of patches 0001-0049 (run 43810802470, artifact 14201150585, verified pin 2779cd7e). The first request (run 43808944773, engine 0001-0048 on base 756) was cancelled before any IPA: an independent review found that 0048's render-target rule never applied to Mario Kart World's terrain tiles. Patches 0048 and 0049: (1) a packaged or CPU-written texture over storage the game drew into before is made with render-target use, the key now learnt on every render-target upgrade (1,687 texture upgrades in 756's log, each a new texture, a copy of every level and every cached texture view sent down the slow path); S2A_RB_RT_STICKY=0 in env.txt restores the upgrade at the first draw; (2) a screenshot's frame capture records every draw (shader keys, each binding with its texture's format, size and channel mapping, vertex attributes, the indirect and multi-draw record) and saves the textures the frame samples, as its shaders read them, on contact sheets (tx-sheet-NN.png, 16 x 16 cells of 128 x 128, with tx-index.txt), so that the red-pink palm trees can be traced to a texture or to a shader from one capture. Patches 0001-0047 are those of 756 and 757; 0048's patch file and README row, deferred by 757, are promoted here. The RPCS3 Core stays the base's (Core 939 request 2); the RPCS3 session's later commits, the MeloNX performance overlay and the RetroAchievements fork gate are source only. MeloNX, XeniaCore, the app (with the NeoPlay stage 2 of 757) and every other retained component are those of the base. Images that must change: S2ArmEngine and Runner. Build-only delivery: Flutter/native groups not-run. Nothing has run on an iPhone; no frame rate, stability or heat claim.",
